  "cut_point": "We are given a round lake with **6 pines** on its shore. These pines are arranged in a **circle**, and we are told that if we select two **triangles**, each formed by three of the pines, such that the first triangle uses three pines and the second triangle uses the other three, then the **treasure** lies at the **midpoint of the segment connecting the orthocenters** of these two triangles.\n\nOur task is to determine how many **dives** one must make to **guarantee** finding the treasure, given that we **do not know** how to divide the six pines into two groups of three (i.e., we do not know which three pines form the first triangle and which three form the second triangle).\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the setup\n\n- There are **6 points (pines)**, equally spaced on the **circumference of a circle**.",
